components.look:
A full-width bar:
- --surface fill, a 1px --divider bottom edge, min-height 4rem;
- padding --space-3 top and bottom, max(1rem, (100% - 70rem) / 2) at the sides;
- flex, wrapping, justify-content space-between, align-items center, gap --space-2 vertical and --space-5 horizontal.

The Brand sits on the left. The nav on the right is a wrapping flex row (gap --space-2 vertical, 1.25rem horizontal) at --text-sm, with min-width 0. It holds:
- 'All reports' and, for the owner, 'Admin' as nav links: --text, weight 500, no underline;
- the Avatar at 24px;
- '.who' ('Signed in as @login'): --text-muted, overflow-wrap anywhere, min-width 0;
- Sign out as a Quiet button.

Signed out, it holds 'All reports' and 'Sign in with GitHub' as a Primary button. .site-header form has margin 0. The markup of the "header" define is byte-unchanged.

nav.admin-nav (aria-label 'Admin'), drawn by the shared "admin-nav" define. It holds three links: Reports (/admin), Blocked users (/admin/blocked) and View site (/).

The nav is the first child of .admin:
- flex 1 1 13rem;
- display flex, flex-wrap wrap, gap .125rem;
- padding 2rem 1rem 0.

Each link:
- display flex, align-items center;
- flex 1 1 calc((20rem - 100%) * 999). This stacks the links in a column while the nav is narrower than 20rem (the desktop sidebar) and lays them in one row when the nav wraps to full width on a phone;
- white-space nowrap, min-height 2.25rem, padding 0 --space-3, --radius-sm;
- --text-sm, weight 500, --text, no underline.

There is no fill and no edge on the nav itself.

The one main action of a page or form, in ink:
- --accent fill, 1px --accent edge, --on-accent text;
- --text-sm, weight 600, line-height --leading-tight;
- min-height --control-h, padding 0 --space-4, --radius-sm, cursor pointer.

Bound to:
- .primary on a button or anchor;
- .signin;
- .comments > form button;
- .reply form button;
- .feedback form button;
- .feedback-inbox form button;
- form[action='/admin/reports'] button.

An anchor (.signin, a.primary) is inline-flex, align-items center, with no underline.

The same metrics as the Primary button, with a --danger fill, a 1px --danger edge and --on-danger text.

Bound to:
- button.danger (buttons only, so .notice.danger never takes it);
- .remove form button;
- .block form button;
- form[action$='/delete'] button.

It is written after the primary rule.

A text-button for summary and button.toggle:
- no fill, no border, padding 0;
- min-height --disclosure-h;
- --text-sm, weight 600, --text-muted.

summary keeps display:flex with align-items center, width fit-content and max-width 100%, list-style none, and a hidden ::-webkit-details-marker. .toggle never sets display; the hidden guard owns it.

The chevron is a ::before:
- content '', display inline-block, flex none;
- a .45em square with 2px right and bottom borders in currentColor;
- rotate(-45deg), so it points right;
- margin-right --space-2.

details[open] > summary::before and .toggle[aria-expanded='true']::before rotate(45deg), so they point down.

input[type=text] and type-less inputs:
- --surface fill, 1px --border, --radius-sm;
- min-height --control-h, padding --space-2 --space-3;
- --text-md, weight 400, --font-sans, --text, line-height --leading-tight;
- max-width 100%.

Inside a Form row it is width 100%. There is no placeholder text.

input[type=file]: --text-sm, --text-muted for 'No file chosen' and for the chosen name, max-width 100%, justify-self start inside a Form row.

Its ::file-selector-button is drawn as a Neutral button:
- --surface fill, 1px --border, --radius-sm;
- min-height --control-h, padding 0 --space-4;
- font inherit at weight 600, --text;
- margin-right --space-3.

Every label wraps its control. label is display grid, with gap --space-2, --text-sm, weight 600 and --text: the label's words sit above the control.

In the upload form:
- each row is a p with margin 0 0 --space-4;
- labels are capped at 32rem;
- the help paragraph (form[action='/admin/reports'] p:not(:has(label, button))) is --text-sm --text-muted.

A refusal by the server is the danger Notice (p.error, role=alert) directly under the page head.

The admin card:
- --surface fill, 1px --divider edge, --radius;
- padding --panel-pad (16px at 375, 24px at 1280);
- no shadow.

A card's first child has margin-top 0 and its last child margin-bottom 0.

Bound to: .panel, dl, form[action='/admin/reports'], .feedback-inbox .feedback-message, .mod and .blocked-account. Cards appear on admin pages only. The reader pages are unboxed.

section.votes in the reading column:
- margin-top --space-7 after the frame;
- padding 1.25rem 0, with 1px --divider top and bottom edges (longhands);
- display flex, flex-wrap wrap, align-items baseline, gap --space-2 vertical and --space-5 horizontal.

.likes and .comment-count are stats: --text-lg, weight 600, --text, tabular-nums, margin 0. .your-vote and .vote-hint follow inline as muted --text-sm hints with margin 0.

The vote form takes flex-basis 100%: a wrapping row of Neutral buttons with gap --space-2 and margin 0.

A block with padding --space-3 --space-4, margin --space-3 0, a 4px left edge, radius 0 --radius-sm --radius-sm 0, and --text text at --text-sm. It never sets display.

Variants:
- neutral (.notice): --surface-2 fill, --text-muted edge;
- danger (.notice.danger, .error): --danger-soft fill, --danger edge;
- success (.notice.ok, .feedback-sent): --ok-soft fill, --ok edge;
- warning (.notice.warning): --warning-soft fill, --warning edge.

**Reader side** (.own-feedback li.feedback-message):
- an unbulleted list;
- each message has a 1px --divider top edge, padding-top --space-4 and margin-top --space-4, a 'You wrote <time>' Byline, and the body.

**The author's reply** (.feedback-reply):
- no fill, a 2px --accent (ink) left edge;
- padding .25rem 0 .25rem --space-4, margin-top --space-3;
- holds the ink Author Badge, a time and the body, like a pull quote.

**Admin side** (.feedback-inbox .feedback-message): each message is a Card holding:
- a Byline (avatar, login, the danger 'blocked' Badge, time);
- its body;
- its author replies (as above);
- a reply form (a Textarea plus the Primary 'Send reply', form margin-top --space-3).

dl as a Card:
- display grid, grid-template-columns max-content minmax(0, 1fr), align-items baseline;
- gap --space-3 vertical and --space-5 horizontal;
- max-width 44rem, margin 0 0 --space-6.

dt: --text-sm, weight 600, --text-muted.
dd: margin 0, min-width 0, overflow-wrap anywhere, tabular-nums, --text. The Status dd holds the Status pill. The SHA-256 dd uses --font-mono at .8125rem.

ul and ol default to padding-left --space-5. The designed lists drop their bullets and padding: .report-list, .own-feedback, .blocked-comments and .blocked-feedback.

In the blocked lists, each li has:
- padding --space-3 0 and a 1px --divider top edge;
- its time as display block, --text-sm, --text-muted;
- its span.body in --text;
- its 'removed' span as the italic muted placeholder;
- its Remove as the Two-step destructive control.

**Page-level** (.empty, main.reader > h1:first-child + p:last-child, .legend + p:last-child):
- --surface-2 fill, --radius;
- padding --space-7 --space-5;
- --text-md, --text-muted, centred.
In reader pages it sits in the 40rem column (margin-left and margin-right auto, margin-top --space-head).

**Inline** (.empty-inline, .no-comments):
- --surface-2 fill, --radius-sm;
- padding --space-3 --space-4, margin --space-2 0 0;
- --text-sm, --text-muted, left-aligned.

layout:
html carries --bg. The Site header spans the full width, with its content inset by max(1rem, (100% - 70rem) / 2).

**Reader pages** (main.reader): main is centred, at most 72rem, padding 1.5rem 1rem 4rem (literal), plus padding-top clamp(2rem, 1rem + 3vw, 4rem) as a longhand.
- At the top, centred in 48rem: the serif display title and the muted meta line (or the legend on All reports).
- The report frame takes the whole 70rem column, like a feature image.
- Everything that is read sits in one centred 40rem column: the votes bar, Feedback, Comments, the branch thread, the All reports list, and the empty states.
- Sections are unboxed, separated by --space-section (48 to 64px) and hairlines.

**Admin pages:** below the header is div.admin, at most 72rem, centred, display flex, flex-wrap wrap, align-items flex-start.
- It holds the Admin sidebar (flex 1 1 13rem) and main[data-hband-admin] (flex 999 1 40rem, max-width none, margin 0, padding 1.5rem 1rem 4rem, padding-top 2rem).
- Each main opens with the Page head (title left, main action right). Below it come the list-first content (the table or cards, 44rem for cards and forms, full width for the table and preview), then secondary sections.

**Other pages** (the Not allowed page): main is centred at 40rem, with padding-top --space-8.

**Vertical rhythm:**
- 48 to 64px between reader sections; 40px from an admin h2 to the previous section; 32px under the admin page head;
- 24px between rows of the All reports list (each row has 24px of padding);
- 16px between cards and between form rows; 12px from a textarea to its button; 8px from a label to its field; 4px from a byline to its body.

**Phone width.** There are no at-rules, so nothing switches at a breakpoint. Everything changes through wrapping and intrinsic sizing:
- the header nav wraps under the brand;
- on admin pages the sidebar wraps above main and becomes one row of three items (the switcher flex-basis);
- the admin page head's action wraps under its title;
- vote buttons, bylines and the All reports meta line wrap;
- type sizes, panel padding, section gaps and table cell padding shrink through clamp(): titles 56px to 34px, sections 64px to 48px, cells 12px to 6px;
- every long word (logins, slugs, the SHA-256, unbroken comment bodies) breaks anywhere.

At 375 the content is 343px wide, a card's inside is 309px, and a level-5 comment keeps 259px (244px at 360). No screen scrolls sideways.
